# Two uses:
#   - Local dev: copy to .env. config.Load reads ./.env at startup, so a bare
#     `go run ./cmd/cadence` picks these up. A variable already set in the
#     environment is never overwritten by this file, so `VAR=x go run
#     ./cmd/cadence` still overrides for one run.
#   - Container: copy to ~/.config/containers/systemd/cadence-cards.env (next
#     to the Quadlet unit, which passes every line to the container as-is).
#     Leave the "local `go run` only" section at the bottom commented out.
#
# Syntax: KEY=VALUE, one per line; `#` comments must be on their own line.
# An unquoted value runs to end of line (no inline-comment stripping). The app
# strips quotes ('#'-containing values need them, e.g. PASSWORD="a#b") but
# Podman's env file does not, so leave values unquoted in the container copy.

# Timezone for SM-2 day-boundary math ("a card is due N days later" uses
# local midnights). Set to your users' timezone.
TZ=UTC

# Claude API (study question generation + chat)
CLAUDE_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-5
CLAUDE_MAX_TOKENS=16000

# Reasoning effort for the tutoring chat: low, medium, high, xhigh, or max.
# CLAUDE_EFFORT=high

# Question generation is a small extraction task; route it to a cheaper/faster
# model and lower effort than the tutoring chat. Empty means "same as
# CLAUDE_MODEL / CLAUDE_EFFORT".
# CLAUDE_QUESTION_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
# CLAUDE_QUESTION_EFFORT=low

# Nightly question pre-generation: a Message Batches job (50% cheaper) runs at
# the first hourly tick at or after QUESTION_PREGEN_HOUR (local time, so TZ
# applies) and pre-generates questions for cards due within 24 hours. Set
# DISABLE_QUESTION_PREGEN=true to opt out of overnight spend.
# DISABLE_QUESTION_PREGEN=false
# QUESTION_PREGEN_HOUR=3

# Allow anyone to register an account. When false, create users with:
#   podman exec -it cadence-cards cadence -create-user you@example.com
ENABLE_PUBLIC_REGISTRATION=false

# --- local `go run` only ---
# Uncommenting DB_PATH and COOKIE_SECURE lets you start with a bare
# `go run ./cmd/cadence`. Keep them commented in the container's env file: the
# image sets PORT and DB_PATH itself, tailscale serve provides HTTPS, and
# rate limiting is the only brute-force defense.
# PORT=3000
# DB_PATH=./dev.db
# COOKIE_SECURE=false         # set false only when serving plain HTTP
# DISABLE_RATE_LIMITING=true  # dev only
